---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const cols = ['Tidemark', 'Plausible', 'Umami', 'Matomo', 'Fathom'];
const rows = [
  ['Hosted version', 'Coming soon', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes'],
  ['Self-host', 'Yes, MIT', 'Yes (Community Edition)', 'Yes, MIT', 'Yes, GPL', 'No'],
  ['Self-hosting needs', 'PHP 8.3+ and a database. Works on shared hosting', 'Docker, Postgres and ClickHouse', 'Node.js and a database', 'PHP and MySQL/MariaDB. Works on shared hosting', '—'],
  ['Cookie-free by default', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Yes', 'Configurable', 'Yes'],
  ['Plausible-style tracking script and API', 'Yes', 'Native', 'No', 'No', 'No'],
  ['Product scope', 'Web analytics, one page', 'Web analytics, one page', 'Analytics, journeys, retention, replay', 'Full analytics suite', 'Web analytics'],
  ['Hosted price', 'Not set yet', 'From $9/mo', 'Free tier, paid plans', 'Paid plans', 'From about $15/mo'],
];
---
<Base title="Tidemark vs Plausible, Umami, Matomo and Fathom" description="How Tidemark compares with Plausible, Umami, Matomo and Fathom: where each runs, what self-hosting takes, and when a different tool is the better choice." crumbs={[{ name: 'Compare', path: '/compare/' }]}>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Tidemark and the alternatives.</h1>
    <p class="lede">All of these are good tools. The real difference is where they run and how much you want to operate. Here is the honest version.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <div class="card tscroll"><table class="t">
      <thead><tr><th><span class="sr-only">Feature</span></th>{cols.map((c, i) => <th class={i === 0 ? 'us' : ''}>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>{rows.map((r) => <tr><th>{r[0]}</th>{r.slice(1).map((c, i) => <td class={i === 0 ? 'us' : ''}>{c}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 0">Based on public information from each project. Products and prices change, so check their pages before you decide, and tell us if something here is out of date.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Choose Tidemark if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You already pay for PHP hosting and want analytics on it, without running Node, Docker or a database cluster.</li>
        <li>You want one calm dashboard and a script that is about 2 KB gzipped.</li>
        <li>You already use Plausible’s script or API and want to point it somewhere you control.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Choose something else if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>You want a managed service today.</strong> Plausible and Fathom are mature, hosted and well run. Tidemark Cloud isn’t open yet.</li>
        <li><strong>You need funnels, retention, session replay or revenue reports.</strong> Umami and Matomo go much further than Tidemark does.</li>
        <li><strong>You need to import years of history.</strong> Tidemark can’t import from other tools yet.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a class="btn primary lg" href={site.downloadUrl}>Download v<span data-ver>{site.version}</span></a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
